  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an array `nums` of integers, a *move* is composed of choosing any element and **decreasing it by 1**.\n\nAn array `A` is a *zigzag array* if either:\n\n* Every even-indexed element is greater than adjacent elements, ie. `A[0] > A[1] < A[2] > A[3] < A[4] > ...`\n* OR, every odd-indexed element is greater than adjacent elements, ie. `A[0] < A[1] > A[2] < A[3] > A[4] < ...`\n\nOutput the smallest number of moves to transform the given array `nums` into a zigzag array.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: We can decrease 2 to 0 or 3 to 1.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [9,6,1,6,2]\nOutput: 4\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
